    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llSetCameraEyeOffset(vector Offset);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Sets the camera eye <b>offset</b> for avatars that sit on the object.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Offset / <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Parameters/offset" target="_blank">offset</a></td>
          <td>offset relative to the prim&#39;s position and expressed in <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Local" target="_blank">local coordinates</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>camera</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">243</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p>This is the position of the camera&#39;s eye, not the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetCameraAtOffset" target="_blank">point it looks at</a>.</p>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Setting this will not update the cameras of seated avatars, it will only effect avatars that subsequently sit down. The camera settings have to be prepared in advance.</li>
    <li>The <b>offset</b> is <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Local" target="_blank">locally relative</a> to the object, if you want it relative to the seated <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Agent" target="_blank">avatar</a> (which likely has a custom sit rotation and offset) or the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Region" target="_blank">region</a>, you must do the computation yourself.</li>
    <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/ZERO_VECTOR" target="_blank">ZERO_VECTOR</a> <b>offset</b> will cancel any eye offset.</li>
    <li>Camera position set by this function is a <b>Prim Property</b>. <b>It will survive the script</b> and it will survive prim taking and prim rezzing</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- Sit the avatar looking at an arbitrary direction
-- Look over the avatar's shoulders from behind once it sits down

local function back_view(degrees)
    local sitRot = ll.AxisAngle2Rot(vector(0, 0, 1), degrees * DEG_TO_RAD)

    ll.SitTarget(vector(0, 0, 0.1), sitRot)

    ll.SetCameraEyeOffset(vector(-2, 0, 1) * sitRot)
    ll.SetCameraAtOffset(vector(2, 0, 1) * sitRot)
end

local function main()
    back_view(208)
    ll.Say(0, "Please sit down")
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// Sit the avatar looking at an arbitrary direction
// Look over the avatar's shoulders from behind once it sits down

back_view(float degrees)
{
     rotation sitRot = llAxisAngle2Rot(<0, 0, 1>, degrees * DEG_TO_RAD);
    
     llSitTarget(<0, 0, 0.1>, sitRot);
        
     llSetCameraEyeOffset(<-2, 0, 1> * sitRot);
     llSetCameraAtOffset(<2, 0, 1> * sitRot);
}

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        back_view( 208 );
        llSay(0, "Please sit down");
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
